{
  "title": "Inline sticky notes merge into instruction text",
  "description": "Some recipe instruction HTML uses inline sticky-note markup \
inside the instruction sentence, and the pipeline flattens the note text \
directly into the instruction body instead of preserving readable spacing or \
dropping the aside.\n\
\n\
Concrete example from \
data/pipeline-snapshots/altonbrown-com_recipes-semi-instant-pancake-mix.json, \
cross-checked against cached HTML at \
~/.ramekin/http-cache/altonbrown-com_recipes-semi-instant-pancake-mix/response.bin:\n\
\n\
The source instruction HTML for `#wprm-recipe-5501-step-0-8` is:\n\
  `<wprm-code><span class=\"sticky-note-btn\">Carefully flip</span><span \
class=\"sticky-note\"><span class=\"sticky-note-text\">The first cakes tend to \
be uglier than later ones, so feed the in-laws first.</span></span> with a \
wide spatula and cook until golden brown on the bottom, another 2 to 3 \
minutes.</wprm-code>`\n\
\n\
The snapshot produces:\n\
  `Carefully flipThe first cakes tend to be uglier than later ones, so feed \
the in-laws first. with a wide spatula and cook until golden brown on the \
bottom, another 2 to 3 minutes.`\n\
\n\
Expected behavior: either preserve the visible instruction text cleanly \
(`Carefully flip with a wide spatula...`) or extract the note in a readable \
way, but do not concatenate hidden/helper note text into the instruction \
sentence without spacing.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "instruction-parser",
  ],
